An existing SQL migration is edited after the fact, and a new one drops a
column. Both change stored data.

=== both package.json
{ "name": "api", "private": true, "main": "src/index.ts" }
=== both src/index.ts
export const ok = true;
=== base db/migrations/0001_init.sql
CREATE TABLE users (id serial PRIMARY KEY, email text NOT NULL);
=== head db/migrations/0001_init.sql
CREATE TABLE users (id serial PRIMARY KEY, email text NOT NULL, name text);
=== head db/migrations/0002_drop_legacy.sql
ALTER TABLE users DROP COLUMN legacy_flag;
DELETE FROM sessions WHERE expired = true;
=== expect
row migration-changed ● title~"`db/migrations/0001_init.sql`" title~"edited"
row migration-changed ● title~"`db/migrations/0002_drop_legacy.sql`" why~"rops column `users.legacy_flag`" why~"deletes rows from `sessions`"
